WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.012 --> 00:00:02.750
(house band instrumentals)

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.320
- All right, welcome back everybody.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.456
Two years ago, my next guest used TikTok

00:00:06.456 --> 00:00:08.280
to land a book deal.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.080
Since then, she released "Lightlark,"

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.099
which became a bestselling,
and soon to be movie.

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:14.456
Now she's back with the sequel,
it's called "Nightbane,"

00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:17.940
and it's one of the most
anticipated young adult novels

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:18.773
of the year.

00:00:18.773 --> 00:00:21.059
Please welcome back to
the show, Alex Aster.

00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:23.892
(audience cheers)

00:00:26.685 --> 00:00:29.685
(instrumental jazz)

00:00:37.744 --> 00:00:39.630
I'm so glad. I love having you back.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.130
- Thank you.
- This is so exciting.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:41.963
- I'm so excited.

00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:43.590
- Your life just keeps
getting better and better.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.360
- It's changed since the
last time I was here.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.699
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:47.532
- Honestly, thanks to your show a lot too,

00:00:47.532 --> 00:00:48.540
so, thank you for having me.
- Oh, no, it's thanks to you.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.950
Girl, look at you're writing.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.210
I love this, so I have to ask.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.641
- [Alex] Yeah.

00:00:52.641 --> 00:00:53.474
- This my favorite thing I learned.

00:00:53.474 --> 00:00:54.900
So, you name your villains and your books

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.463
off of people you don't like?

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:58.673
- So I.

00:00:58.673 --> 00:01:00.360
- You should have been a
songwriter, I'm just saying.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.014
- So, Kelly, I follow the
Taylor Swift rule of writing.

00:01:03.014 --> 00:01:04.057
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:04.057 --> 00:01:06.396
- If you do not want a song,
or a book, written about you,

00:01:06.396 --> 00:01:08.880
don't be mean. Don't be
mean to writers. (laughs)

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.835
- Yeah, that'd your fault. That's on you.

00:01:10.835 --> 00:01:12.574
(audience cheers)

00:01:12.574 --> 00:01:15.480
- Yeah, in reality, I always need names.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.710
Like, when you're writing a book.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:17.855
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:17.855 --> 00:01:19.382
- Sometimes you use a filler name.

00:01:19.382 --> 00:01:20.215
And so, I just, kind of, thought one day,

00:01:20.215 --> 00:01:21.048
"Hmm, I need a, a name for the villain."

00:01:21.048 --> 00:01:22.740
And, I was like, "I don't
really like that person.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.110
Maybe, they would be the good
person to like fit in there."

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:25.943
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:25.943 --> 00:01:27.331
- They don't usually end
up in the final copy.

00:01:27.331 --> 00:01:29.490
One, because I don't wanna be sued.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.459
And. (laughs)
- You are smart, as well.

00:01:31.459 --> 00:01:34.179
- And, two, because their names
are never that interesting.

00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:36.781
Like, I write fantasy, so
you can't have, like, a Chad

00:01:36.781 --> 00:01:39.124
be the villain of like a fantasy book.

00:01:39.124 --> 00:01:41.880
- Because Chad wears a
puca shell necklace. Yeah.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.136
- (laughs) Yeah.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.676
It's not, like, competing
in a deadly games, so, yeah.

00:01:44.676 --> 00:01:45.757
So, I usually do change it,

00:01:45.757 --> 00:01:47.100
but it's a habit that I've developed,

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.221
and I post a lot about it.

00:01:48.221 --> 00:01:50.760
And so, the funny part is
that thousands of people

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.940
will comment on my posts
with name suggestions.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:54.820
- Oh my God. They're like, "please!"

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.720
- Yes, "please!" Like, "Julie,"
or, like, they'll just name.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.370
So, I have a whole list of names.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.420
I don't even need to think about people

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.710
in my own life anymore.
- That's very helpful.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.660
- Yes.
- Well, catch us up

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:04.950
on the series. What's going on right now?

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.427
- So, for anyone that isn't familiar,

00:02:06.427 --> 00:02:08.460
"Lightlark" is about
an island that appears.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.611
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:09.611 --> 00:02:10.444
- Once every hundred years

00:02:10.444 --> 00:02:11.843
to host a game where six rulers fight

00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:14.130
to break their deadly curses.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.121
So, to break them all, one
of the six rulers has to die

00:02:16.121 --> 00:02:18.450
and one will win unmatched power.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.150
So, there's adventure,
romance, big plot twist.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.203
You don't know who's lying
until the very last page,

00:02:23.203 --> 00:02:25.950
and "Nightbane," the next
book, which is out now,

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.930
starts exactly where "Lightlark" ends.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.125
So, you can almost read
it like a giant book.

00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:30.958
- Yes!

00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:32.730
- And, like the last
time I was here, I said

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:35.010
it's being made into a
movie franchise by Universal

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.740
and the people behind a
very big young adult series

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.330
that you might know.
- That's amazing.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:40.950
- [Alex] Yeah!
- I'm so excited for you.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.480
- Yeah, I'm so excited too.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.223
I was here exactly a year ago,

00:02:44.223 --> 00:02:46.163
and it was just the
beginning of "Lightlark,"

00:02:46.163 --> 00:02:48.045
and now "Nightbane," is coming out,

00:02:48.045 --> 00:02:49.321
so it's really a full circle moment.

00:02:49.321 --> 00:02:50.525
- Oh my God.
(audience claps)

00:02:50.525 --> 00:02:51.907
Wait, so what was your
like favorite genre,

00:02:51.907 --> 00:02:53.430
like, growing up, what was
your favorite book genre?

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.230
- My favorite book genre growing up

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.245
was the genre I'm writing
in now, young adult fantasy.

00:02:57.245 --> 00:02:59.203
- [Alex] That makes sense.

00:02:59.203 --> 00:03:01.245
- So, my favorite book was
"Twilight," growing Up.

00:03:01.245 --> 00:03:02.344
- [Kelly] Oh, I love that.

00:03:02.344 --> 00:03:03.603
- That was the first
book that I ever read,

00:03:03.603 --> 00:03:04.740
that I was like, "wow,
reading can be really fun."

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.300
And so, I set out to write books

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.590
that could really be escapist,

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.390
and like, get people out
of their normal world.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:10.590
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- So, that's what I write now.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.060
- Get people interested
in reading, as well.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.645
- [Alex] Yes, exactly!

00:03:13.645 --> 00:03:15.078
- 'Cause a lot of people
like the young adult fantasy,

00:03:15.078 --> 00:03:16.150
that kind of thing.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:16.983
So, yeah.

00:03:16.983 --> 00:03:17.816
- Yes. Adults read it too.

00:03:17.816 --> 00:03:18.649
- Yeah.
- Like, most of the.

00:03:18.649 --> 00:03:19.800
- Oh, I read all that too, yeah.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.633
- [Alex] Yeah. (giggles)

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.080
- My mother and I are big into that.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.485
We always.
- [Alex] I love that.

00:03:23.485 --> 00:03:24.318
- I love a series.
- [Alex] Yes!

00:03:24.318 --> 00:03:25.544
- I hate When it's one
book, I'm like. (groans)

00:03:25.544 --> 00:03:26.541
- Now you can read both books.

00:03:26.541 --> 00:03:27.374
- [Kelly] I know.

00:03:27.374 --> 00:03:28.377
- And, like, just combine them both, yeah.

00:03:28.377 --> 00:03:29.399
- I love that. I love a series.

00:03:29.399 --> 00:03:31.560
So, I heard that you also said

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.830
Gen-Zers are, like,
different types of readers.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.450
- Yes.
- What do you mean?

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.060
- I think that people think
that now with social media,

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.835
people's attention spans,
and like kids aren't reading.

00:03:40.835 --> 00:03:41.668
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:41.668 --> 00:03:42.840
- But, now in the last few years,

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:43.797
it's honestly the opposite.

00:03:43.797 --> 00:03:44.630
And, it's kind of funny,

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.240
because social media is
getting people reading.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.440
So, my books were
discovered on social media

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.343
and so many more millions of
books are being discovered,

00:03:51.343 --> 00:03:53.325
and these people now are becoming readers.

00:03:53.325 --> 00:03:54.158
Like you said,

00:03:54.158 --> 00:03:56.430
you just need one book
to get you into reading.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:57.263
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:57.263 --> 00:03:58.096
- And, then you're a lifelong reader.

00:03:58.096 --> 00:03:59.272
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:00.162
- So, people are discovering
my books on social media

00:04:00.162 --> 00:04:01.380
and they're becoming readers.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.974
So, it's really interesting
how social media now

00:04:02.974 --> 00:04:04.336
is making people read.

00:04:04.336 --> 00:04:07.020
Whereas, I think the public perception

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.720
is that Gen Z isn't reading,
but they're reading now

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.010
more than ever, book sales are up.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.449
So it's great.
- Yeah.

00:04:12.449 --> 00:04:13.474
- [Alex] Yeah.

00:04:13.474 --> 00:04:15.068
- It is interesting
too for any generation.

00:04:15.068 --> 00:04:16.680
I just think it has to be
something you're interested in.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:17.513
- [Alex] Yes.
- Right?

00:04:17.513 --> 00:04:19.657
Because my sister, even we
were talking about this today,

00:04:19.657 --> 00:04:21.021
and, you know, we're both over 40.

00:04:21.021 --> 00:04:21.971
- [Alex] Yeah.

00:04:21.971 --> 00:04:22.890
- And, she was like, "You know,
I never really liked reading

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.660
until you showed me," and I
don't know if it was Jane Austen

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.286
or Jane Eyre or something that
was as an author of the book.

00:04:27.286 --> 00:04:28.119
- Yeah.

00:04:28.119 --> 00:04:28.952
- But, I don't know which one it was,

00:04:28.952 --> 00:04:30.200
but she was like, "It really got me in."

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.110
- [Alex] Yes.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:31.943
- And then, that thing opened up.

00:04:31.943 --> 00:04:34.080
Now, she reads more books

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.790
than I'll ever eat in my entire life.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:36.623
- You just need that one book.

00:04:36.623 --> 00:04:38.061
- I'm like, "how do you have
the time?" I'm like, yeah.

00:04:38.061 --> 00:04:39.901
- I know, and so, I was
honestly writing the books

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:41.000
that I wanted to read.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.243
And so that's like how I started.

00:04:42.243 --> 00:04:44.100
- That's the best thing to do.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.030
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:46.350
That's like how I wanna make shows.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.250
They're like, "You should do a show".

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.630
And, I'm like, "but I wanna
make one I wanna watch."

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.463
- Yes.

00:04:49.463 --> 00:04:51.150
I think that when it
starts from that place,

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.123
it can always be good because
there's people like you

00:04:53.123 --> 00:04:54.960
who would wanna read it or watch it.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:55.793
- Absolutely. It's relatable.

00:04:55.793 --> 00:04:56.824
So, do your fans come up
with theories for your books?

00:04:56.824 --> 00:04:58.950
Do you get like, as well as names,

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:00.240
do they often send you ideas?

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.317
- Yes.

00:05:01.317 --> 00:05:04.200
And, actually only two people know, like,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.960
how the series ends, and
I have to keep it a secret

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.790
because I'm just so afraid
that people will know.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.590
Like there's a love triangle in the book

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.650
and people are very fiercely
like Team Oro or Team Grim.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.510
And so, people wanna know
who she ends up with.

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:16.343
- Yeah.

00:05:16.343 --> 00:05:17.176
- So, I really, I have
to keep it a secret.

00:05:17.176 --> 00:05:18.360
As much as I share on social media,

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.040
I have to keep some stuff secret

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.389
- [Kelly] Oh, absolutely.
- About the plot.

00:05:22.389 --> 00:05:23.571
- My mother's the worst.

00:05:23.571 --> 00:05:24.404
My mother, when you said the last page,

00:05:24.404 --> 00:05:25.440
you find out on the last page.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.352
My mother starts at the
last page. I'm not kidding!

00:05:28.352 --> 00:05:30.531
- [Alex] Oh no.
- She has a giant spoiler.

00:05:30.531 --> 00:05:31.560
She's like, "Oh, I just went to the end

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.393
to see what they're."

00:05:32.393 --> 00:05:33.560
- And, I was like, "well
you missed the whole ride!"

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.256
It's like the whole, I was
like, "It drives me nuts."

00:05:35.256 --> 00:05:36.509
But, she does that,

00:05:36.509 --> 00:05:38.209
so I'm gonna tell her not
to start with the last page.

00:05:38.209 --> 00:05:39.042
- Yeah.

00:05:39.042 --> 00:05:42.240
- Do you have any advice
for, like, aspiring writers?

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:43.530
Because you came in the industry

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:44.940
in a very different way?
- Yes.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.040
- Yeah.
- I always say never give up.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.900
I started writing books
when I was 12 years old.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.142
This has been my dream
since I was a child.

00:05:50.142 --> 00:05:51.450
And, it just, it didn't work.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.280
I got hundreds of
rejections with every book.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.573
And, this book, "Lightlark,"
was rejected by 16 publishers.

00:05:55.573 --> 00:05:57.721
Almost every single single
publisher rejected it.

00:05:57.721 --> 00:05:59.880
And, now it's been in New
York Times best seller

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:00.750
for over a straight year.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.130
So, like, you just never know.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:02.963
You gotta find someone who believes in it.

00:06:02.963 --> 00:06:04.430
- You can't, it's because of the readers.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.282
They did this.

00:06:05.282 --> 00:06:07.128
So, as long as you put yourself out there,

00:06:07.128 --> 00:06:10.162
you don't need to wait for
the gatekeepers to let you in.

00:06:10.162 --> 00:06:11.976
You can truly, especially
now with social media

00:06:11.976 --> 00:06:14.940
and self-publishing, you
can create your own destiny.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.027
And so, I truly advise
anyone who's writing,

00:06:17.027 --> 00:06:18.540
just put your work out there.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.460
You never know what's gonna happen.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.293
- Absolutely.

00:06:21.293 --> 00:06:22.650
And, it's interesting you
mentioned Taylor earlier.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:23.618
- [Alex] Yeah.

00:06:23.618 --> 00:06:25.994
- She, well there's been a
lot of Taylors on the show.

00:06:25.994 --> 00:06:27.441
(Alex laughs)

00:06:27.441 --> 00:06:28.492
But, it's interesting,

00:06:28.492 --> 00:06:30.242
'cause I remember hearing in
Nashville, she got turned down

00:06:30.242 --> 00:06:31.900
by so many people, and then
finally got her opportunity.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.331
And that's, what, she's
biggest star on the planet.

00:06:34.331 --> 00:06:36.000
You just need one "yes."

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.050
- Yeah, you need one "yes."

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:38.470
And, you need a team that believes in it.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:39.570
- Yes, exactly.
- Yeah, I agree with that.

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.520
And, I think it's a really
cool thing to tell people, too.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.755
- Yeah.

00:06:42.755 --> 00:06:44.175
- Because people can give
up or get disheartened.

00:06:44.175 --> 00:06:45.175
- Yes.

00:06:45.175 --> 00:06:46.179
- You know, pretty easily.
- Yeah.

00:06:46.179 --> 00:06:47.197
- Especially creative people.

00:06:47.197 --> 00:06:48.195
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:06:48.195 --> 00:06:49.197
Well, alright, "Nightbane,"

00:06:49.197 --> 00:06:50.070
the sequel to the bestselling
book, "Lightlark,"

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:50.903
is available now.

00:06:50.903 --> 00:06:52.200
Y'all gotta go check it out.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.033
Get a copy.

